  "cost_comparison_caveats": {
    "headline_ratio_is_not_measurable": "The SDK worker's INPUT AMPLIFICATION is well evidenced (input_cached 6.96M vs input 2.89M, from per-turn conversation re-send plus a ~11.5k-token identity preamble). The TIER RATIO is NOT measurable from this telemetry. Neither this run's nor the sibling run's headline ratio should be quoted as an SDK-vs-API or SDK-vs-Opus result.",
    "reasons": [
      "Asymmetric measurement: under auth_mode=estimated the 3 opus phases are a char/3.8 ESTIMATE priced from the policy pricing block; the 27 flash packets carry VENDOR-REPORTED tokens.",
      "LARGEST UNDERSTATEMENT: senior-reviewer and security-reviewer each ran full Opus sessions and emitted NO cost event, so they are absent from the $1.0404 opus figure entirely. Only architect is captured (as the change_plan event).",
      "Orchestrator overhead is unbilled to any packet: verification runs, git inspection, scope checks, provenance bookkeeping and gate relays appear in no telemetry event. Real premium-tier spend exceeds $1.0404.",
      "Gemini 3.7 Flash rates are UNCONFIRMED: the policy carries TODO(pricing) with input 1.50 / input_cached 0.15 / output 9.00. Every flash figure scales linearly with those numbers."
