  "findings": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "severity": "high",
      "title": "The plan enumerated one full-PUT caller; there were two",
      "detail": "FR-D2 was written to prevent a whole-task round-trip silently clearing the field, and it DID prevent it for the web fetcher. But apps/api/src/mcp/tools.ts buildFullTaskUpdateBody is a SECOND read-merge-full-PUT caller and was not enumerated, so every MCP-driven task edit would have written NULL over the estimate. Found by security review; missed by both the design and the senior review.",
      "lesson": "A design that mandates round-tripping a field through a full-document endpoint owes a COMPLETE INVENTORY of that endpoint's callers. The lesson is the enumeration gap, not the missing line.",
      "scope_note": "Distinct from the brief's non-goal. 'No MCP tool exposure' meant do not add a NEW MCP capability. This was an EXISTING tool destroying user data. Declining a feature is not declining to prevent data loss.",
      "status": "FIXED (tp_026) + regression test (tp_027, 5 cases incl. null-vs-undefined)"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "severity": "medium",
      "title": "The repo's pre-commit hook does not typecheck",
      "detail": ".husky/pre-commit is `set -e; pnpm exec biome ci .; pnpm run build`. pnpm run build is turbo build, and apps/web's build is `vite build` — no tsc. vitest does not typecheck either. A package that does not compile therefore passes the hook.",
      "evidence": "Demonstrated concretely in this run: 385 API + 132 web tests were green at a moment when apps/web had 7 typecheck errors.",
      "status": "PRE-EXISTING, out of scope, not fixed. Worth a maintainer's attention."
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "severity": "medium",
      "title": "CORRECTION TO THE ORCHESTRATION INSTRUCTION: `pnpm --filter <pkg> test -- <path>` silently runs the entire suite",
      "detail": "The run instruction mandated verifying packets with `pnpm --filter <pkg> test -- <path>`. The `--` is consumed before vitest ever sees the path, so the filter is dropped and the FULL suite runs. Verified directly: with `--` -> 39 files / 132 tests; without `--` -> 1 file / 10 tests.",
      "correction": "Correct form is `pnpm --filter <pkg> test <path>` with NO double-dash. (`pnpm --filter <pkg> exec vitest run --config vitest.config.ts <path>` also works.)",
      "why_it_matters": "This is the same trap that killed a packet on the sibling branch — reproduced inside the very instruction written to prevent it. Workers tp_019/tp_020/tp_021 did NOT disobey; they ran the command given and it ran everything. No packet was lost here only because these suites are ~30s. Confirmed fixed: tp_027 used the no-double-dash form and correctly reported 1 file / 5 tests.",
      "status": "RECORDED AS AN INSTRUCTION CORRECTION, not a worker fault."
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "severity": "low",
      "title": "Unformatted reference code in a design doc propagates into the codebase",
      "detail": "change_plan.md section 2.5 carried a reference implementation that was itself unformatted. Codegen copied it verbatim — correct worker behaviour — and apps/web/src/lib/estimate.ts consequently failed biome ci on formatting.",
      "lesson": "Run the formatter over reference snippets embedded in design documents.",
      "status": "FIXED via targeted `biome format --write` on exactly the 5 affected paths; never the repo-wide lint script (which is `biome check --write` and rewrites unrelated files)."
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
